$\mathrm{Bi}_2 \mathrm{O}_3$ is the most basic oxide because of higher reactivity with acid.

\mathrm{Bi}_2 \mathrm{O}_3+6 \mathrm{HCl} \rightarrow 2 \mathrm{BiCl}_3+3 \mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{O}

$\mathrm{Al}_2 \mathrm{O}_3$ and $\mathrm{Sb}_2 \mathrm{O}_3$ are amphoteric and $\mathrm{SeO}_2$ is acidic.
